/* SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT */
/* SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Daniel Gardiner d/b/a FractalSQLabs
 *
 * Function registry for FSQ protocol v2. X(sql, kind, cls) per row. kind:
 * STR (STRING result), INT (INTEGER result), REAL (REAL result). sql is the
 * bare C identifier that CREATE FUNCTION ... SONAME 'fractalsql.so' names,
 * and the name a client sends in UDF_INIT and UDF_CALL (see SPEC.md). There
 * is no numeric opcode per function. The shim and the daemon both get this
 * table through scripts/gen_udf.py, so there is one source.
 *
 * cls classifies what a re-execution after a dropped-mid-flight call costs
 * (see SPEC.md's retry section). The daemon ignores it; the shim table
 * carries it:
 *   r -- pure: no side effects, deterministic; safe to transport-retry with
 *        a fresh request (vector, dimensions, search inputs, portfolio
 *        math, topology geometry, and the read-only ledger/audit probes).
 *   s -- stateful: mutates daemon state (diversify params, sessions,
 *        feedback, the ledger, the audit log); NOT retried with a fresh
 *        request -- the shim may resend once carrying the same idempotency
 *        token so the daemon can replay a cached result (SPEC.md).
 *   e -- expensive/external: a provider round trip the caller pays for
 *        (reasoning, embeddings, LLM text-to-SQL generation). A dropped
 *        call surfaces an error; retry is the caller's choice.
 */

/* Search and discovery */
X(fractal_search, STR, r)
X(fractal_search_explore, STR, r)
/* Dimension, analytics, and informational */
X(fractal_version, STR, r)
